          "id": "id",
          "emoji": "🇮🇩",
          "label": "Indonesia"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "hi",
      "explain": "India. The night is Sharad Purnima, called Kojagiri Purnima in Maharashtra — the full moon of the month of Ashwin, usually in October. Kojagiri means \"who is awake\": the night is spent in prayer to Lakshmi, with kheer set out under the moonlight and shared the next day as prasad, and the moon of this night is said to show all sixteen of its parts. The same full moon: reunion and mooncakes on one side, a vigil and a sweet in the moonlight on the other."
