      "question_id": "q-20260829-sidang-isbat",
      "date": "2026-08-29",
      "kind": "guess",
      "topic_id": "top_01KZXQ6BSDEE4S0X0YWV3Y6E2Z",
      "topic_slug": "ramadan-and-eid",
      "asker_locale": null,
      "target_locale": null,
      "text": "Guess: in which community is the first day of Ramadan announced only after the government meets the evening before, weighing crescent sightings against the calculation?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "id",
          "emoji": "🇮🇩",
          "label": "Indonesia"
        },
        {
          "id": "hi",
          "emoji": "🇮🇳",
          "label": "India"
        },
        {
          "id": "zh-CN",
          "emoji": "🇨🇳",
          "label": "China"
        },
        {
          "id": "en",
          "emoji": "🇺🇸",
          "label": "the United States"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "id",
      "explain": "Indonesia. The Ministry of Religious Affairs convenes a sidang isbat the evening before, weighing crescent reports from dozens of stations across the country against the calculation, and only then declares whether the next day is the first. For 1447 AH (2026) the session met on 17 February; the crescent stood below the horizon at every station, and the session settled on 19 February by calculation. So a confirmed answer to \"what date does fasting start\" is, by design, unavailable months ahead — while the Eid break is scheduled a year in advance by joint decree of three ministries."
    },
